<v Sklar Brothers>[INAUDIBLE] is 6' 4", and de Blasio is 6' 5". So you can say, now I'm standing up here, you can see that I'm not as tall as these guys. But I went to Trump's doctor-- I went to Trump's doctor, and he said I was 6 foot 3.
<v Sklar Brothers>[听不清]是6英尺4英寸，德布拉西奥是6英尺5英寸。所以你可以说，现在我站在这里，你可以看到我不像这些家伙那么高。但我去了特朗普的医生那里——我去了特朗普的医生那里，他说我有6英尺3英寸。

00:23:37.370 --> 00:23:40.880
<v Sklar Brothers>[LAUGHTER]
<v Sklar Brothers>[笑声]

00:23:40.880 --> 00:24:13.570
<v Ira Glass>The Sklars went through jokes, all of them pretty mean, about candidates Booker, de Blasio, Ryan, Moulton, Klobuchar, and Inslee. And can I just say, respect for anybody who can make a joke about Moulton, Ryan, or Inslee? None of these jokes are going to make the cut, Castro's staff tells me later. Those kinds of jokes just aren't Castro's style. The one joke they could imagine the candidate actually telling onstage at the debate-- I have to say, it really surprised me-- the one about how he's kind of short.
<v Ira Glass>斯克拉兄弟讲了一堆笑话，所有这些关于布克、德布拉西奥、瑞安、莫尔顿、克洛布查和英斯利候选人的笑话都相当刻薄。我能说吗，尊重任何能拿莫尔顿、瑞安或英斯利开玩笑的人？卡斯特罗的员工后来告诉我，这些笑话一个都不会被采用。那种笑话根本不是卡斯特罗的风格。他们能想象候选人真正会在辩论台上讲的那一个笑话——我不得不说，这真的让我很惊讶——关于他个子有点矮的那一个。

00:24:13.570 --> 00:24:23.020
<v Ira Glass>Of course, the other thing that Julián has to practice is reacting to all the other candidates and the moderators. They study videos of his opponents, and they do this.
<v Ira Glass>当然，胡利安必须练习的另一件事是对所有其他候选人和主持人的反应。他们研究对手的视频，并这样做。

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:29.650
<v Millie>Hello, and welcome to sunny Miami, Florida, for the first Democratic debate of the 2020 presidential cycle. I'm Rachel Maddow.
<v Millie>你好，欢迎来到阳光明媚的迈阿密，佛罗里达州，参加2020年总统周期的第一次民主党辩论。我是瑞秋·马多。

00:24:29.650 --> 00:24:30.770
<v Sawyer Hackett>I'm a lot of people.
<v Sawyer Hackett>我是很多人。

00:24:30.770 --> 00:24:48.560
<v Ira Glass>It's a mock debate session. Sawyer and a staffer named Millie play the moderators. Four other staffers stand at podiums flanking Castro's. The men are now in ties and jackets. They want to give Castro the chance to run his answers under debate conditions where he's going to have to wait for his opponents to speak, where he might have to field answers that kind of poke at him.
<v Ira Glass>这是一个模拟辩论环节。索耶和一个名叫米莉的员工扮演主持人。另外四名员工站在卡斯特罗两侧的讲台上。男人们现在打着领带，穿着夹克。他们想给卡斯特罗一个机会，在辩论条件下进行回答，他将不得不等待对手发言，他可能不得不应付那种有点挑衅他的回答。

00:24:48.560 --> 00:25:08.530
<v Ira Glass>And I have to say, it was totally charming and fascinating how accurate they tried to be at playing the other candidates in the debate. Out on the road, they've watched these politicians deliver the same lines again and again. So when Derek, who is playing Cory Booker, gets a question about gun violence, he has Booker's lines down cold.
<v Ira Glass>我不得不说，他们试图表现得准确地扮演辩论中的其他候选人是非常迷人且令人着迷的。在路上，他们看了这些政治家一遍又一遍地重复同样的台词。所以当德里克，扮演科里·布克时，被问及关于枪支暴力的问题，他把布克的台词背得滚瓜烂熟。

