<v Derek Eadon>I've been waking up in the middle of the night hearing gunshot. I released my policy not far from where Shahad Smith had been killed.
<v Derek Eadon>我半夜醒来能听到枪声。我在离沙哈德·史密斯被杀地点不远的地方发布了我的政策。

00:25:14.770 --> 00:25:25.240
<v Ira Glass>When a staffer playing Beto O'Rourke is asked about Castro's ability to connect with Latinos and to speak Spanish-- apparently, Castro is not as good at Spanish as Beto is-- fake Beto responds fully in character.
<v Ira Glass>当扮演贝托·奥罗克的员工被问及卡斯特罗与拉美裔联系和讲西班牙语的能力时——显然，卡斯特罗的西班牙语没有贝托说得好——假贝托完全入戏地回应。

00:25:25.240 --> 00:25:43.210
<v Staffer>Look, Lester, I think it's pretty offensive that you and others continue to say that just because someone doesn't speak Spanish means they can't connect with the Latino vote. There's many ways to connect it. For example, Amy and I are still living in El Paso. I've grown up my entire life there. And so I know the unique challenges that our border community faces.
<v Staffer>听着，莱斯特，我认为你和其他人继续说仅仅因为某人不讲西班牙语就意味着他们无法与拉美裔选票建立联系，这相当令人反感。有很多联系的方式。例如，艾米和我还住在埃尔帕索。我一生都在那里长大。所以我知道我们的边境社区面临的独特挑战。

00:25:43.210 --> 00:26:02.230
<v Ira Glass>In the mock debate, Castro does a relaxed, solid job deploying the answers that he's been working on. But he also gets to practice interrupting other candidates. And this is important because, again, he is worried that other candidates might hog the stage, and he won't get much time or many questions directed at him. And Castro told me that his natural inclination is not to interrupt.
<v Ira Glass>在模拟辩论中，卡斯特罗在部署他一直在研究的答案时表现得轻松、扎实。但他也得到了练习打断其他候选人的机会。这很重要，因为，再说一次，他担心其他候选人可能会垄断舞台，而他得不到太多时间或指向他的问题。卡斯特罗告诉我，他的自然倾向不是打断别人。

00:26:02.230 --> 00:26:22.930
<v Julian Castro>I mean, for me, I'm not naturally the guy in a group that has to talk all the time, like they would call gunners in law school. You know gunners? People that would, in law school classes, that basically would be the ones always trying to answer the question that a professor would throw out. That's not me.
<v Julian Castro>我的意思是，对我来说，我自然不是一群人中那种必须一直说话的人，就像他们在法学院被称为“枪手”那样。你知道“枪手”吗？那些在法学院课堂上，基本上总是试图回答教授提出的问题的那些人。那不是我。

